#: website/web/templates/about.html:13
msgid "About RansomLook"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:15
msgid ""
"Open-source project providing real‑time ransomware intelligence: tracked "
"groups, posts, mirrors, forums, and more."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:26
msgid "What is RansomLook?"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:28
msgid ""
"RansomLook is an open‑source project aimed at assisting users in tracking"
" ransomware‑related posts and activities across various sites and forums."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:31
msgid "The main components include:"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:33
msgid "Blog monitoring and victim extraction"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:34
msgid "Forum monitoring (parsing is not available)"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:35
msgid "Overview of Ransomware Notes"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:36
msgid "Tracking leaks from public sources"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:37
msgid "Leak tracking from RecordedFuture provider (private API required)"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:38
msgid "Monitoring of various known Bitcoin wallets"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:46
msgid "Who uses RansomLook?"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:47
msgid "RansomLook is built for, and used by:"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:49
msgid ""
"<strong>SOC / IR teams</strong> — spotting victims in real time, "
"correlating outbound traffic with known ransomware mirrors during "
"incident response."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:50
msgid ""
"<strong>CTI analysts</strong> — tracking group activity, emergence of new"
" actors, infrastructure churn, and producing trend reports."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:51
msgid ""
"<strong>CSIRTs / national CERTs</strong> — building situational awareness"
" and notifying constituents when they appear in a leak post."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:52
msgid ""
"<strong>Security researchers</strong> — studying the ransomware ecosystem"
" over time via open data and the API."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:53
msgid ""
"<strong>Journalists</strong> — verifying claims, confirming victim "
"disclosures, and grounding reporting in public evidence."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:61
msgid "Getting started"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:62
msgid "Start from the page that matches your use case:"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:64
msgid ""
"<strong>Incident response</strong> → <a href=\"/recent\">/recent</a> "
"&nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href=\"/urls\">/urls</a> (check if a URL you observed "
"matches a tracked mirror)."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:65
msgid ""
"<strong>CTI / trend analysis</strong> → <a href=\"/stats\">/stats</a> "
"&nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href=\"/hot\">/hot</a> (trending groups)."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:66
msgid ""
"<strong>Directory / lookup</strong> → <a href=\"/browse\">/browse</a> "
"(all groups, markets, actors)."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:67
msgid ""
"<strong>Automation / integration</strong> → <a href=\"/doc/\">API "
"documentation</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href=\"/rss.xml\">RSS feed</a>."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:68
msgid ""
"<strong>Self-hosting</strong> → <a "
"href=\"https://github.com/RansomLook/RansomLook\" target=\"_blank\" "
"rel=\"noopener\">GitHub repository</a> (Docker compose &amp; Poetry "
"instructions in the README)."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:76
msgid "Data freshness"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:78
msgid ""
"RansomLook scrapes tracked DLS / forums on a continuous loop — mirror "
"availability, post lists and screenshots are refreshed multiple times per"
" day. The <a href=\"/\">homepage</a> shows the live <em>last 7 days</em> "
"delta so you can judge activity at a glance; <a "
"href=\"/stats\">/stats</a> exposes the full aggregation controls."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/about.html:81
msgid ""
"Sources are open-by-design: we track what is publicly claimed on leak "
"sites. Claims from operators are <strong>not</strong> independently "
"verified against victim confirmations — always treat a post as a "
"<em>claim</em> until corroborated elsewhere."
msgstr ""

