#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:9
msgid ""
"Technical terms used across RansomLook: groups, actors, infrastructure "
"types, metrics and relationships."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:18
msgid "Table of contents"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:19
msgid "Sections"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:21
#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:31
msgid "Core concepts"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:22
#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:51
msgid "Infrastructure types"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:23
#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:83
msgid "Data and metrics"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:24
#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:107
msgid "Ecosystem and sources"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:25
#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:127
msgid "Relationships"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:35
msgid ""
"A ransomware group or data-extortion collective tracked by RansomLook. "
"Groups usually operate one or more leak sites, file servers and "
"communication channels."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:38
msgid "Actor"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:39
msgid ""
"A named individual or pseudonym (threat actor, developer, affiliate, "
"broker, admin, etc.) related to ransomware or data-extortion activity."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:42
msgid "Victim / Post"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:43
msgid ""
"A single entry published by a group about a targeted organisation. In "
"RansomLook this is usually stored as a \"post\" and is associated with "
"one group and one discovery timestamp."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:47
msgid ""
"Ransomware-as-a-Service. Operating model where a core team develops the "
"ransomware and infrastructure, while affiliates perform intrusions and "
"share the profits."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:54
msgid "DLS"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:55
msgid ""
"Dedicated Leak Site / Darknet Leak Site. Tor-based website operated by a "
"group to list victims and publish stolen data when ransoms are not paid."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:58
msgid "FS"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:59
msgid ""
"File Server / File Storage. Infrastructure used to host or distribute "
"stolen data (archives, samples, full dumps)."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:62
msgid "Chat"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:63
msgid ""
"Communication endpoints used for negotiation or contact with victims and "
"affiliates. Includes web-based chat, Telegram, X/Twitter, email and other"
" messaging."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:66
msgid "Admin / Affiliates panel"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:67
msgid ""
"Administrative or affiliate-focused infrastructure not intended for "
"public victim browsing. Recruitment panels, campaign portals, status "
"pages."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:70
msgid "Relay / Mirror"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:71
msgid ""
"A technical copy of a group's site accessible at a different domain or "
"onion address. RansomLook tracks each relay as a separate location with "
"its own status."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:74
msgid "Slug"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:75
msgid ""
"Normalised name used internally to build URLs for a specific location of "
"a group. Used to create deterministic filenames and links."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:78
msgid "Private location"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:79
msgid ""
"A location stored in the database but not displayed to unauthenticated "
"visitors. Still used for scraping, monitoring and metrics."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:86
msgid "Parser"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:87
msgid ""
"Piece of code dedicated to a specific group or site. Extracts structured "
"data from HTML pages (victim name, sector, country, dates, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:90
msgid "Discovery date"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:91
msgid ""
"Timestamp at which RansomLook first observed a victim post. May differ "
"from the original intrusion or encryption date."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:94
msgid "Leak / Dataleak"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:95
msgid ""
"Public dataset containing credentials or other information exposed in "
"previous breaches. RansomLook integrates external leak databases for "
"enrichment."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:98 website/web/templates/group.html:204
msgid "Ransom notes"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:99
msgid ""
"Text files or HTML pages left on compromised systems by ransomware "
"operators. RansomLook indexes ransom notes to help identify families and "
"operations."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:102
msgid "Crypto address / Wallet"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:103
msgid ""
"Cryptocurrency address controlled or used by a group or affiliate to "
"receive ransom payments. Monitored and correlated with known activity."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:111
msgid ""
"Darknet or clearnet platforms where actors trade access, data, tools or "
"services. Tracked as separate entities from ransomware groups."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:115
msgid ""
"Optional Recorded Future integration providing additional leak "
"information and dumps. Requires a private API key."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:118
msgid "Onion service (Tor)"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:119
msgid ""
"Hidden service accessible through the Tor network. Most DLS, FS and "
"negotiation panels are onion services, sometimes with multiple relays."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:122
msgid "v3 onion"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:123
msgid ""
"Current version of Tor hidden service addresses (56-character "
"<code>.onion</code> domains). RansomLook tracks versions to classify "
"infrastructure changes."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:130 website/web/templates/group.html:416
#: website/web/templates/group.html:419 website/web/templates/group.html:420
msgid "Affiliates"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:131
msgid ""
"External operators who work with a core ransomware group. Perform "
"intrusions, deploy ransomware and share a percentage of the ransom."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/admin/torrent_health.html:74
#: website/web/templates/admin/torrent_health_detail.html:91
#: website/web/templates/admin/torrent_health_detail.html:142
#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:134
msgid "Peers"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:135
msgid ""
"Other actors linked to a given individual. Can represent collaboration, "
"shared infrastructure or repeated co-appearance in operations."
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:138
msgid "Groups / Forums relations"
msgstr ""

#: website/web/templates/glossary.html:139
msgid ""
"Links between one actor and multiple groups or markets. RansomLook stores"
" these so users can explore which actors operate across which ecosystems."
msgstr ""

